      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this correct when called in the middle of 2 queries ? If 10s have passed, the base delay is 20s and there\u0027s no backoff, shouldn\u0027t this method return 10s ?\n\nI feel that it would all be simpler if you also keep a lastSentTime member in the QueryTask, and do something like:\n\n\n    private long calculateNextSendTime(@NonNull QueryTask lastScheduledTask, boolean lastTaskWasSent, long now) {\n        final long lastSentTime \u003d lastTaskWasSent ? now : lastScheduledTask.lastSentTime;\n        final long baseDelayInMs \u003d lastScheduledTask.config.delayUntilNextTaskWithoutBackoffMs;\n    \tif (!lastScheduledTask.config.shouldUseQueryBackoff()) {\n    \t    return lastSentTime + baseDelayInMs;\n    \t}\n        final long minTtl \u003d getMinRemainingTtl(now);\n    \tif (minTtl \u003c\u003d 0) {\n    \t    // There\u0027s no service, or there is an expired service. In any case, schedule for the minimum\n    \t    // time, which is the base delay.\n    \t    return lastSentTime + baseDelayInMs;\n    \t}\n    \tfinal long timePassed \u003d now - lastScheduledTask.timeWhenScheduled;\n    \tif (!lastTaskWasSent \u0026\u0026 (lastScheduledTask.minRemainingTtlWhenScheduled - timePassed \u003d\u003d minTtl)) {\n    \t    // Use the original scheduling time if the TTL has not changed, to avoid continuously\n    \t    // rescheduling to 80% of the remaining TTL as time passes\n    \t    return lastScheduledTask.nextQueryTaskRunTime;\n    \t}\n        return Math.max(now + (long) (0.8 * minTtl), lastSentTime + baseDelayInMs);\n    }\n    \n - On initial scheduling, if hadReply from cache, create the same QueryTask that would be used if there\u0027s no cached value,\n   and call with lastTaskWasSent\u003dtrue\n - Otherwise, create a QueryTask with lastSentTime\u003dnow\n - On query received, call with lastTaskWasSent\u003dfalse. If return value \u003c\u003d lastScheduledTask.nextQueryTaskRunTime, don\u0027t reschedule\n - After sending a query, call with lastTaskWasSent\u003dtrue",
